abstract: >-
  A documentary apparatus for the battle of Manzikert (26 August 1071) and
  the Byzantine civil war that followed it, 1068-1072, built from
  public-domain sources carried in whole sections, with the original beside
  a working English translation: the eyewitness Michael Attaleiates
  (Greek, Bonn 1853, pp. 138-180, set from two OCRs and read against the
  page images); Psellos' Chronographia (Sathas 1899) and Bryennios' Hyle
  Historias (Bonn 1836), the palace's and the Doukas family's versions;
  Ibn al-Athir's year 463 (Arabic, Tornberg 1864, transcribed by eye);
  Matthew of Edessa (Dulaurier's French, 1858) and Michael the Syrian
  (Chabot's French, 1905); and Gibbon's chapter 57 (1788) as reception,
  corrected against the first edition. With a timeline, plates, a Compare
  page setting the seven voices side by side, and an explicit list of what
  is not carried and why, above all Sibt ibn al-Jawzi, whose only edition
  is not public domain. Companion game: The Turned Standard.
keywords:
